1. SOC 2 ( this can be implemnted at terraform configurations setting this permissions and we can check using checkov)

SOC 2 = Service Organization Control 2.

It is an auditing framework used to evaluate whether a company has appropriate controls for protecting customer data and operating its systems securely.

For example, a SaaS company may need controls around:

🔐 Access control — only authorized employees can access production.
📝 Logging & monitoring — important actions are recorded.
🔒 Encryption — data is protected in transit and at rest.
👤 Identity management — MFA, IAM, least privilege.
💾 Backup & recovery — systems and data can be recovered.
🚨 Incident response — procedures exist for security incidents.
🔄 Change management — production changes are reviewed and tracked.


PCI-DSS = Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard. ( avoid storing raw card numbers (PAN) if you don't need to. Use a PCI-compliant payment provider/tokenization so your application handles a token instead of the actual card number where possible.)
